WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:04.560
With studios eager to build as much hype as
possible before their films are released,

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:07.770
March has been a fire sale month for new movie
trailers.

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:09.140
"Oh, my God!

00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:11.820
We're having a fire… sale.

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:13.180
Oh, the burning!

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:14.920
It's burning me!"

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:20.260
Over the course of the month, we saw new trailers
for high-profile releases like Infinity War,

00:00:20.279 --> 00:00:24.280
Deadpool 2, and Fantastic Beasts: The Crimes
of Grindelwald, along with some exciting first

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:28.480
looks for upcoming films like the Sicario
sequel and Action Point, to name a few.

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:33.190
With so many movies big and small on their
way to theaters in 2018, it's a lot to go

00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:34.190
through.

00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:37.899
Here's a look at the trailers released in
March 2018 for films that we're getting excited

00:00:37.899 --> 00:00:40.010
about.

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:41.010
Wildling

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:45.829
From IFC Midnight, Wildling is a horror thriller
about a young girl named Anna who's thrust

00:00:45.829 --> 00:00:49.960
into the modern world after spending her whole
life being raised by her father in the woods.

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:54.440
She's put in the care of a police officer,
played by Liv Tyler, who soon realizes that

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:56.180
there's something strange about the girl.

00:00:56.180 --> 00:01:01.039
In particular, Anna can't seem to shake her
fear of a local legend about a ferocious beast

00:01:01.039 --> 00:01:02.449
called the Wildling.

00:01:02.449 --> 00:01:06.960
There's a lot to take in from the trailer,
which sort of hints that Anna may be the mysterious

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:07.960
Wildling.

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:10.450
"He ate all the other children.

00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:13.450
You're the last one left."

00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:17.460
Hopefully that isn't the movie's main plot
twist, but even if it turns out to be, Wildling

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:19.679
at least looks like an enjoyable ride.

00:01:19.679 --> 00:01:23.549
Wildling hits theaters and video-on-demand
services on April 13th.

00:01:23.549 --> 00:01:26.229
Avengers: Infinity War

00:01:26.229 --> 00:01:30.240
With another full-length trailer for Infinity
War released this March, Marvel is definitely

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:31.729
cashing in on the hype.

00:01:31.729 --> 00:01:35.919
Set to an emotional rendition of the original
Avengers theme, the newest trailer hints at

00:01:35.919 --> 00:01:39.959
a plan to make Thanos come to the Avengers'
home field to secure his Infinity Stones,

00:01:39.959 --> 00:01:43.959
and of course offers more glimpses of the
epic superhero team-ups we're all waiting

00:01:43.959 --> 00:01:44.959
for.

00:01:44.959 --> 00:01:48.259
Tony Stark and Peter Parker hash out a plan
with Peter Quill and Drax.

00:01:48.259 --> 00:01:50.529
Captain America hitches a ride with T'Challa.

00:01:50.529 --> 00:01:52.899
Thor brings the lightning with Rocket and
Groot.

00:01:52.899 --> 00:01:55.729
It's like getting all the ice cream flavors
on one cone.

00:01:55.729 --> 00:01:58.209
Well, minus whatever the Hawkeye flavor is.

00:01:58.209 --> 00:01:59.529
Very Berry?

00:01:59.529 --> 00:02:03.819
Look for Avengers: Infinity War on April 27th.

00:02:03.819 --> 00:02:04.829
Terminal

00:02:04.829 --> 00:02:06.229
What is this movie about?

00:02:06.229 --> 00:02:10.649
The teaser gives nothing away, which is, admittedly,
what teasers are supposed to do.

00:02:10.649 --> 00:02:14.170
Most of the visuals simply show a pair of
feet in high heels walking down a candlelit

00:02:14.170 --> 00:02:15.209
aisle.

00:02:15.209 --> 00:02:19.519
Margot Robbie headlines Terminal, and her
voice over in the trailer hints at dark happenings.

00:02:19.519 --> 00:02:23.140
Mike Myers and Simon Pegg are also slated
to star in the film, although their roles

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:26.080
are still just as much a mystery as the rest
of Terminal.

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:30.159
This train's riding into the station on May
11th.

00:02:30.159 --> 00:02:31.650
Deadpool 2

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:35.719
Deadpool 2's trailers have all revealed something
new, and this one sees Deadpool putting together

00:02:35.719 --> 00:02:38.900
the X-Force team - with plenty of action along
the way.

00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:42.959
While the first trailer was mostly filled
with jokes about the film's CG and writing,

00:02:42.959 --> 00:02:46.819
this one touches on the story a little more,
revealing that Cable is on a mission involving

00:02:46.819 --> 00:02:51.150
Julian Dennison's character and giving a little
more screen time to the new cast of mutants.

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:57.060
At this point, we're all definitely hyped
for Deadpool's second coming on May 18th.

00:02:57.060 --> 00:02:58.060
Action Point

00:02:58.060 --> 00:03:01.909
Judging by the trailer, Action Point will
lie somewhere between a scripted film and

00:03:01.909 --> 00:03:03.640
a Jackass stunt showcase.

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:08.250
The film draws from the real-life Action Park,
a notorious New Jersey waterpark.

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:09.780
"I love it!"

00:03:09.780 --> 00:03:12.640
"There's nothing i the world like Action Park!"

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:18.880
The park featured such attractions as Cannonball
Loop, a rickety waterslide that began with

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:24.969
a steep 45-degree drop and ended in a bone-crunching
full 360-degree loop before ejecting patrons

00:03:24.969 --> 00:03:28.829
onto a plastic tarp being sprayed down by
an employee with a garden hose.

00:03:28.829 --> 00:03:31.249
Yeah, it was that kind of waterpark.

00:03:31.249 --> 00:03:35.299
So it should be no surprise that Johnny Knoxville
honed in on Action Park as the subject for

00:03:35.299 --> 00:03:36.510
his newest movie.

00:03:36.510 --> 00:03:41.010
It's the perfect canvas for painful, epic
stunts, and with Jackass mainstays like Chris

00:03:41.010 --> 00:03:44.560
Pontius along for the ride, we're just crossing
our fingers that the movie production suffers

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:46.600
fewer casualties than the park itself.

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:48.060
"Let's see what this baby can do!"

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:53.159
Take the ride on June 1st.

00:03:53.159 --> 00:03:54.159
Tag

00:03:54.159 --> 00:03:57.810
Go ahead and and make all the Hawkeye jokes
you want, but you can't deny that Tag looks

00:03:57.810 --> 00:03:59.200
like a fun film.

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:02.860
The story centers on five friends who have
spent most of the last 30 years playing the

00:04:02.860 --> 00:04:08.280
same game of tag, for one month every year,
they engage in a no-holds-barred game of "you're

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:11.560
it," ignoring all social conventions while
the game is on.

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:12.840
Wedding ceremony?

00:04:12.840 --> 00:04:13.920
Funeral for a father?

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:17.440
It doesn't matter as long as they can get
within tapping distance of each other.

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:20.959
"I think your dad would have really wanted
you to be… it!"

00:04:20.959 --> 00:04:26.220
Believe it or not, Tag is actually based on
a true story about a group of friends who

00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:28.620
have been doing this exact same thing for
decades.

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:30.960
It's not all lighthearted playground antics,
either.

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:35.280
It was this film, and not Infinity War, that
saw Renner break both of his arms performing

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:36.550
a stunt.

00:04:36.550 --> 00:04:39.259
That's a little more hardcore than getting
together with your old friends for a game

00:04:39.259 --> 00:04:40.389
of Yahtzee.

00:04:40.389 --> 00:04:43.500
The game begins on June 15th.

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:45.389
Under the Silver Lake

00:04:45.389 --> 00:04:49.900
From David Robert Mitchell, the guy who brought
us 2015's It Follows, Under the Silver Lake

00:04:49.900 --> 00:04:54.340
is a surreal neo-noir mystery comedy about
a young man in L.A. who starts searching for

00:04:54.340 --> 00:04:55.919
clues about a woman's disappearance.

00:04:55.919 --> 00:04:59.900
The deeper he digs, the more he begins to
believe that there's a secret code embedded

00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:04.060
in the world's media, with everything from
pop songs to cereal boxes hiding messages

00:05:04.060 --> 00:05:05.460
for him to decode.

00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:09.979
From the looks of the trailer, Under the Silver
Lake will be a swan dive into paranoia, centered

00:05:09.979 --> 00:05:14.500
on a man who may have discovered the world's
biggest, darkest secret...or, he might just

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:15.500
be crazy.

00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:19.770
Either way, the trailer promises plenty of
suspense, violence, and conspiracies, all

00:05:19.770 --> 00:05:21.449
wrapped up in a quirky comedy.

00:05:21.449 --> 00:05:24.990
Under the Silver Lake hits theaters on June
22nd.

00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:26.979
Sicario: Day of the Soldado

00:05:26.979 --> 00:05:33.139
2015's Sicario raked in huge amounts of critical
praise for its unflinching portrayal of Mexico

00:05:33.139 --> 00:05:37.430
in the grip of a cartel war, although it wasn't
exactly the kind of movie that screamed for

00:05:37.430 --> 00:05:38.430
a sequel.

00:05:38.430 --> 00:05:42.360
Day of the Soldado will see Josh Brolin and
Benicio del Toro reprising their roles from

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:43.580
the first film.

00:05:43.580 --> 00:05:47.840
Their job in Soldado is to push the Mexican
cartels into a full-on war, no matter who

00:05:47.840 --> 00:05:50.170
gets caught in the crossfire.

00:05:50.170 --> 00:05:51.440
"You're gonna help us start a war."

00:05:51.440 --> 00:05:52.440
"With who?"

00:05:53.340 --> 00:05:54.340
"Everyone."

00:05:55.140 --> 00:05:58.020
Denis Villeneuve, who helmed the first film,
won't be returning as director.

00:05:58.020 --> 00:06:02.349
The reigns are instead going to Stefano Sollima,
an Italian director whose previous credits

00:06:02.349 --> 00:06:08.629
include 2015's Suburra and the TV series Gomorrah,
both of which focus heavily on organized crime.

00:06:08.629 --> 00:06:11.979
In other words, he should be a good match
for the Sicario brand.

00:06:11.979 --> 00:06:16.560
And with a script from Taylor Sheridan, screenwriter
of the original, Sicario: Day of the Soldado

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:19.340
ought to be just as powerful as its predecessor.

00:06:19.340 --> 00:06:22.229
Look for it in theaters on June 29th.

00:06:22.229 --> 00:06:24.460
The House with a Clock in its Walls

00:06:24.460 --> 00:06:28.949
As a director, Eli Roth is best known for
movies like Cabin Fever, Hostel, and The Green

00:06:28.949 --> 00:06:31.730
Inferno , you know, not the kind of stuff
you'd take your kids to.

00:06:31.730 --> 00:06:36.250
So it may be surprising that Roth is set to
direct this upcoming children's fantasy film.

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:39.970
The story centers on a young boy who moves
in with his uncle, who enlists the boy to

00:06:39.970 --> 00:06:43.780
help him find a magical clock in the house
that has to power to bring about the end of

00:06:43.780 --> 00:06:44.780
the world.

00:06:44.780 --> 00:06:48.810
In the trailer, we get our first look at Jack
Black as the uncle and Cate Blanchett as the

00:06:48.810 --> 00:06:50.750
powerful witch who lives next door.

00:06:50.750 --> 00:06:54.879
From the looks of it, The House with a Clock
in its Walls is turning into a slightly creepier

00:06:54.879 --> 00:06:56.439
A Series of Unfortunate Events.

00:06:56.439 --> 00:07:00.909
And with Steven Spielberg's production company
Amblin Entertainment behind the film, it should

00:07:00.909 --> 00:07:02.389
be a whole lot of fun.

00:07:02.389 --> 00:07:04.949
Look for it on September 21st.

00:07:04.949 --> 00:07:07.080
Fantastic Beasts: The Crimes of Grindelwald

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:11.440
Newt Scamander is traveling to Paris in the
latest trailer for Fantastic Beasts: The Crimes

00:07:11.440 --> 00:07:15.580
of Grindelwald, where he apparently bumps
into a young, handsome Albus Dumbledore, played

00:07:15.580 --> 00:07:16.580
by Jude Law.

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:20.330
Dumbledore recruits Scamander to help him
put a stop to Grindelwald's plans.

00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:24.500
This looks like the start of a magical journey
that will traverse the globe and, of course,

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:28.190
feature plenty of fantastic beasts to both
help and hinder our heroes.

00:07:28.190 --> 00:07:32.479
From new shots of Johnny Depp as Grindelwald
to several scenes inside Hogwarts, the trailer

00:07:32.479 --> 00:07:36.509
offers just enough to give Potterfiles a thrill
of excitement.

00:07:36.509 --> 00:07:41.199
Fantastic Beasts: The Crimes of Grindelwald
apparates into theaters on November 16th.

00:07:41.199 --> 00:07:42.220
Thanks for watching!

00:07:42.220 --> 00:07:44.409
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:07:44.409 --> 00:07:47.050
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

